An lcov report from `cargo llvm-cov --lcov` is converted, annotated, and written
as a Cobertura report where `report` writes one (a dry run says where). The lcov
file is never the one written.

```
$ jci-coverage complexity --file coverage/report.lcov --dry-run
[..]INFO jci_coverage::complexity: complexity [..]
complexity: 9 methods in the report, 8 after merging 1 duplicate instantiation(s)
  8 matched, 0 not matched to a source function
  total 12, mean 1.50, max 3
  most complex:
       3  demo::block_on::<demo::later::{closure#0}>
       2  demo::pick::<u8>
       2  demo::total::{closure#0}
       2  demo::later
       1  demo::never
  0 function(s) at or over complexity 10, 0 at or over CRAP 30
(dry run) would write coverage/cobertura.xml

```
